Make the virtual IP usable the moment it is installed.

A Windows address goes through duplicate address detection before it is
usable. Until DAD finishes it is Tentative, and a Tentative address cannot be
bound to: ICMP already flows from it, but every TCP connect over the tunnel
fails. The desktop app has to wait that out after charon reports the tunnel up
(`wait_for_virtual_ip` in vpn-desktop/src/backend.rs, which binds a socket to
the address in a loop), and that wait was a large part of why a connect took
ten seconds on Windows and about one on macOS, where utun addresses need no
DAD.

There is nothing to detect. The Wintun adapter is created for this tunnel and
is point-to-point: nothing else is on its link to collide with. So:

  kernel-iph add_ip()        installs the address with DadState =
                             IpDadStatePreferred, as Wintun's own example and
                             WireGuard for Windows do;
  wintun set_iface_mtu()     zeroes the adapter's DadTransmits while it already
                             writes the interface row, so no address on it is
                             ever held back -- add_ip() calls set_mtu() on the
                             device before it installs the address.

diff -ru orig/src/libcharon/plugins/kernel_iph/kernel_iph_net.c work/src/libcharon/plugins/kernel_iph/kernel_iph_net.c
--- orig/src/libcharon/plugins/kernel_iph/kernel_iph_net.c	2026-10-19 17:04:33.461321717 +0000
+++ work/src/libcharon/plugins/kernel_iph/kernel_iph_net.c	2026-10-19 17:04:33.494571035 +0000
@@ -863,6 +863,14 @@
 	row.PreferredLifetime = INFINITE;
 	/* the whole point is to source tunnelled traffic from this address */
 	row.SkipAsSource = FALSE;
+	/* Usable at once, not after duplicate address detection. The adapter is
+	 * ours alone and point-to-point, so there is nothing to collide with --
+	 * but until DAD finishes the address is Tentative, and while it is no
+	 * socket can bind to it: the tunnel answers ping and refuses every TCP
+	 * connect, for seconds after it reported up. Wintun's own example adds
+	 * its address exactly this way (and the adapter's DadTransmits is zeroed
+	 * in the wintun plugin, for the same reason). */
+	row.DadState = IpDadStatePreferred;
 
 	ret = CreateUnicastIpAddressEntry(&row);
 	if (ret != NO_ERROR)
diff -ru orig/src/libstrongswan/plugins/wintun/wintun_device.c work/src/libstrongswan/plugins/wintun/wintun_device.c
--- orig/src/libstrongswan/plugins/wintun/wintun_device.c	2026-10-19 17:04:33.462759969 +0000
+++ work/src/libstrongswan/plugins/wintun/wintun_device.c	2026-10-19 17:04:33.494742102 +0000
@@ -370,6 +370,10 @@
 			 this->if_name, waited);
 	}
 	row.NlMtu = mtu;
+	/* no duplicate address detection on this adapter: nothing else is on
+	 * its link, and a Tentative address cannot be bound to -- see add_ip()
+	 * in kernel-iph, which installs the virtual IP right after this */
+	row.DadTransmits = 0;
 	/* has to be cleared when writing an IPv4 row back, otherwise the call
 	 * fails with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER */
 	row.SitePrefixLength = 0;
